# Line endings, settled here rather than left to each machine's git config.
#
# Without this, a checkout on Windows converts every text file to CRLF, and
# Prettier — which is configured for LF and is right to be, since that is what
# the repository holds — then reports every one of them as misformatted. That
# turns the Windows half of the release build into a failure about nothing.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` normalises on the way in and checks out LF everywhere, so
# the working tree matches the repository on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries git must not touch. It guesses well, but a corrupted icon or font
# discovered at package time is a guess not worth relying on.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.wasm binary
